      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFixes #62135. \n\nCurrently, requesting `moe_backend=\"cutlass\"` with online FP8 raises a bare `ValueError` without stating the reason or alternatives. This PR updates `select_fp8_moe_backend` to use `_make_log_unsupported` for the CUTLASS branch and explicitly list the supported alternative backends.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Fixes the error message for CUTLASS FP8 MoE backend rejections to include the specific reason and list of supported alternatives.\n- Aligns the CUTLASS error reporting with sibling backends (like HUMMING).\n\n## Validation\n\n- Validated locally by triggering the error path with an unsupported configuration. The error now correctly prints the supported alternatives.\n- Test command run: `pytest tests/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/oracle/test_fp8.py`\n\n## Details\n\nThe root cause is a hardcoded `raise ValueError` at `oracle/fp8.py:468` that bypassed the `_make_log_unsupported` helper used by other backends in the same function. The change simply routes the CUTLASS rejection through the existing reporting helper to improve startup UX.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
